        "title": "Glycolysis and Gluconeogenesis",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Glycolysis (\"sugar splitting\") is the ancient, universal, **cytosolic** pathway\nthat cleaves one 6-carbon glucose into two 3-carbon pyruvate molecules. It needs no\noxygen, runs in essentially every cell, and is the on-ramp to the rest of energy\nmetabolism. The structure is a **deferred-payoff investment**: spend 2 ATP up\nfront to destabilize glucose, then recover 4 ATP on the back end."
    },
